{"id":"word:hebrew:H2719","type":"word","title":"חֶרֶב","subtitle":"H2719 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"drought ; also a cutting instrument (from its destructive effect), as a knife , sword , or other sharp implement","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to חֶרֶב (H2719) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-f.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 413 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"חֶרֶב (chereb) means drought ; also a cutting instrument (from its destructive effect), as a knife , sword , or other sharp implement First listed occurrence: 1Chr 5 18."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"חֶרֶב","transliteration":"chereb","pronunciation":"kheh'-reb","strong":"H2719","lemmaId":"hebrew:H2719","partOfSpeech":"n-f","forms":["חֶ֔רֶב","חָ֑רֶב","חָֽרֶב","בַּ/חֶ֣רֶב","חֶ֖רֶב"],"morphs":[["HNcfsa",150],["HRd/Ncfsa",103],["HTd/Ncfsa",28],["HNcfsc/Sp3ms",18],["HNcfsc",16],["HC/Ncfsa",14],["HR/Ncfsa",12],["HNcfsc/Sp1cs",11],["HNcfsc/Sp2ms",8],["HR/Ncfsc",8]]},"definitions":{"short":"drought ; also a cutting instrument (from its destructive effect), as a knife , sword , or other sharp implement","usage":"axe, dagger, knife, mattock, sword, tool.","full":"H2719. chereb חֶ֫רֶב 411 noun feminine Isa 21:15 sword (as weapon; Aramaic חַרְבָּא , , Zinjirli חרב ; Arabic dart, javelin ) — absolute חֶ֫רֶב Gen 3:24 +; חָ֑רֶב Exod 17:13 +; construct חֶ֫רֶב Deut 33:29 +; suffix חַרְבִּי Exod 15:9 13 t.; חַרְבְּךָ Gen 27:40 7 t.; חֵרְבֶּ֑ךָ 1Sam 17:33 ; Psa 17:13 ; חַרְבּוֺ Num 22:23-24 t.; חַרְבְּכֶם Jer 2:30 ; Ezek 33:26 ; חַרְבָּם Psa 37:15 ; 44:4 ; plural חֲרָבוֺת Isa 21:15 5 t.; construct חַרְבוֺת Josh 5:2 2 t.; suffix חַרְבוֺתָיו Ezek 26:9 ; חַרְבוֺתָם Isa 2:4-5 t.; חַרְבֹתֵיהֶם Micah 4:3 2 t.; — 1. a. sword , as weapon of war Gen 48:22 (E), Judg 7:14 , 20 ; 1Sam 21:9 , and so in all periods; two-edged (short) sword ׳ח אָרְכָּהּ גֹּמֶד פֵיוֺ֖ת שְׁנֵי וְלָהּ Judg 3:16 , compare ׳ח מִּיּוֺת Prov 5:4 (in simile), ׳ח מִּיפִיּוֺת Psa 149:6 ; see also ח ׳צוּר edge of sword 89:44 . b. gird on sword = הח ׳חָגַר 1Sam 17:39 ; 25:13 (3 t. in verse); Psa 45:4 ( יָרֵך עַל ׳ח ׳הח ), ירך על שִׂים Exod 32:27 , compare especially 2Sam 20:8 . c. draw the sword הח ׳הֵרִיק Exod 15:9 ; Lev 26:33 ; Ezek 5:2 , 12 ; 12:14 ; 28:7 , הח ׳הוציא 21:8 ; 21:10 , הח ׳פתח Psa 37:14 ; Ezekiel 21:33, נטשׁ Isa 21:15 (Gr Che לטשׁ see below); usually הח ׳שׁלף Num 22:23 , 31 ; Josh 5:13 ; Judg 3:22 ; 8:10 , 20 ; 9:54 ; 1Sam 17:51 ; 31:4 = 1Chr 10:4 ; 21:16 , and as characteristic of warriors ח ׳שֹׁלֵף Judg 20:2 , 15 , 17 , 25 , 35 , 46 ; 2Sam 24:9 ; 2Kin 3:26 ; 1Chr 21:5 (twice in verse); אֶלהַֿח יָדוֺ ׳וַתִּדְבַּק 2Sam 23:10 , insert also in || 1Chr 11:13 (Dr). d. whet, sharpen the sword הח ׳לטשׁ Psa 7:13 (compare Isa 21:15 above), but also שׁנן Deut 32:41 compare Psa 64:4 , הוּחַדָּה Ezek 21:14 ; 21:16 . e. put up the sword into the sheath הח ׳הֵשִׁיב אֶלנְֿדָנָהּ 1Chr 21:27 ( sheath of sword is elsewhere תַּעַר 1 Samuel 7:51; 2Sam 20:8 ; Jer 47:6 ; Ezek 21:8 ). f. slay with sword ׳בח הרג Josh 10:11 ; 13:22 +; in אנשׁים ימותו 1Sam 2:33 , insert בְּחֶרֶב before ᵐ5 אנשׁים We Dr; rarely בח ׳הכה Josh 11:10 ; 2Kin 19:37 = Isa 37:38 ; very often לְפִיחֿ ׳הִכָּה smite according to the mouth of the sword i.e. as the sword can devour ( 2Sam 2:26 ; 11:25 ) = without quarter Num 21:24 (E) Deut 13:16 ; a 20:13 ; Josh 11:11-12 , 14 (all D) Judg 18:27 ; 21:10 ; 1Kin 10:25 ; Job 1:15 , 17 ; also with העיר as sole object Josh 8:24 ; 10:28 , 30 , 32 , 35 , 37 , compare 10:39 ; 19:47 ; Judg 1:8 , 25 ; 20:37 ; 1Sam 22:19 (twice in verse); 2Sam 15:14 ; לפיחֿ ׳הרג Gen 34:26 (J); לפיחֿ ׳החרים Deut 13:16 b (including הָעִיר in object), Josh 6:21 ; 1Sam 15:8 , לפיחֿ ׳חלשׁ Exod 17:13 (E); לפיחֿ ׳נפל Josh 8:24 ; Judg 4:16 ; י ׳ל֗֗֗פיחֿ׳וַיָּהָם 4:15 ; &#8212; ( ׳לפיחֿ is chiefly in Joshua and Judges (21 t.), in Hexateuch only J E D; but Job post-exilic). g. הח ׳אכלה etc., of the sword as devouring: — בָשָׂר חַרְבִּי תּאֹכֵל Deut 32:42 (poetry), 2Sam 2:26 ; 11:25 ; 18:8 ; Isa 1:10 ; Jer 2:30 ; 46:10 , 14 ; Nahum 2:14. h. slain by sword is ׳חֲלַלחִֿ Num 19:16 (P) and frequently Ezekiel, ׳חַלְלֵיחֿ Ezek 31:17-18 , 32:21 , 25 , 28 , 29 , 30 , 32 ; 35:8 ח ׳מְחֻלְלֵי Ezekiel 35:26 &lt; Co ׳חלליחֿ (on text of 32:20 , 22 , 31 see Co). i. ח ׳שְׁבֻיוֺת Gen 31:26 are captives of (taken by) sword . j. sword frequently agent of ׳י Judg 7:20 ; Isa 34:6 ; Jer 12:12 ; 47:6 etc., — so Deut 28:22 , but read חֹרֶב see below I. חרב (compare on other hand 1Sam 17:47 ); note especially Gen 3:24 הַמִּתְהַמֶּכֶת הח ׳לַהַט ; in poetry ח ׳לַהַכ Nahum 3:3 , ח ׳בְּרַק Deut 32:41 . k. ׳ח figurative of tongue Psa 57:5 ; compare 59:8 ; figurative of violence war, etc., Gen 27:40 ; in simile Prov 5:4 (of grievous end of dealings with strange women). 2 knife ׳ח צֻרִים flint knives for use in circumcision Josh 5:2-3 ,(see We Skizzen iii, 166 ); Ezek 5:1-2 , הַגַּלָּבִים ׳ח תַּעַר חַדָּה (according to Co use of sword as razor is significant). 3 of tools used in hewing stone עליה הֵנַפְתָּ חַרְבְּךָ Exod 20:25 ; בח ׳יִתֹּץ Ezek 26:9 , according to most = tools , axes, 'steel' (Co ' Eisen ' ), but possibly swords as implement ready to hand; 2Chr 34:6 Qr בְּחַרְבֹתֵיהֶם with their tools ; read perhaps בְּחָרְבֹתֵיהֶם in their ruins , Be, who compare Psa 109:10 ; see חָרְבָּה below II. חרב ( ᵑ9 ᵐ5 omit חרב ).","rootNote":"from 2717 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 5 18","keyReferences":["1Chr 5 18","1Chr 10 4","1Chr 10 4","1Chr 10 5","1Chr 21 5","1Chr 21 5","1Chr 21 12","1Chr 21 12"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":413,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 5 18","book":"1Chr","chapter":5,"verse":18,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/חֶ֨רֶב֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ncfsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 10 4","book":"1Chr","chapter":10,"verse":4,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"חַרְבְּ/ךָ֣","source":"he